,"title":"MXLNote","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other."}]}}}